                <pb facs="0817" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg723"/>

                <head>No. 467.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Manning.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 11,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Reports concerning executions at Nogales have been most conflicting since 6th
                    instant. Your telegram announcing appeal is just received with satisfaction.
                    This Government would view with deep regret the imposition of a penalty so
                    extreme, and you are instructed to say that a mitigation would be regarded by us
                    with favor.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
